    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0446" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 702.6811/44.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Attorney General to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of Justice</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to say that, as requested
                    in your letter of the 28th ultimo, the Department has instructed the United
                    States Attorney at Philadelphia to call the attention of the judge of the United
                    States District Court for the Eastern District of Pennsylvania to the provisions
                    of Article VI of the Convention of July 11, 1903,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d483-f1"
                    /> with Greece (33 Stats. 2126), guaranteeing the inviolability of consular
                    offices, and to suggest the apparent advisability of the dissolution of the
                    order enjoining the Greek Consul at Philadelphia to hold certain papers
                    transmitted to him by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, pending the further
                    direction of the Court.</p>
                <closer>For the Attorney General: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Marvin Underwood</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d483-f1" n="3" xml:id="d483-f1-content">
                <p>Date of proclamation of the Consular Convention of Nov. 19, 1902.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
